For all my custom plugins I added the following property `isReady: true`:
```
app.registerPlugin({
      id: PLUGIN_ID,
      initializer: Initializer,
      isReady: true, <- this resolved the issue
      name: PLUGIN_ID
    });
});
```

This resolved the infinite loading.

I to am having the same issue. Glad I am not the only one as I thought it was something to do with my proxy config. Applying a patch to @strapi/admin to not use lodash set in 5.7.0 fixes it. I don't know if there is any other side effects from it though. Not an ideal solution. I have no custom local plugins and this is on a fresh install just for testing this exact issue. I did replicate some of my other production config by adding s3 provider, import-export, and advanced-uuid plugins through npm. I can test with a super fresh install, but really it doesn't matter because plugins are pretty much necessary in an actual production use. I will also try upgrading to 5.8.0.

EDIT:
After more testing, removing telemetryDisabled: true or setting it to false may or may not have had an impact. In my very unscientific test, I went from getting the loading screen 95% of the time to getting the loading screen 75% of the time. Applying a patch to @strapi/admin completely fixes it. There must be something wrong with the way lodash is working. :/

