For anyone that happens to come across this and doesn't know how to apply a patch in an npm project:
npm install patch-package
mkdir patches
touch @strapi+admin+5.8.0.patch
(copy above into that new file)
in your package.json
```json
"description": "A Strapi application",
  "scripts": {
    "build": "strapi build",
    "deploy": "strapi deploy",
    "develop": "strapi develop",
    "start": "strapi start",
    "strapi": "strapi",
    "postinstall": "patch-package"    // <----- add this
  },
  "dependencies": {
```

Now when you run npm install, this will apply the patch to the package. When building a docker container, remember to include the patches folder in the app root of the container along side the package.json file before you run npm install && npm build && npm prune --production

